    <article class="owners-guide">

      <header style="margin-bottom:2rem;padding-bottom:1.5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)">
        <span class="section-label">Your site is live</span>
        <h2 style="border-bottom:none;padding-bottom:0">Welcome to your new website.</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:0.5rem">Here's a two-minute read explaining what we've set up, what we'll handle, and how to reach us.</p>
      </header>

      <h3>What's live</h3>
      <p>Your site is now live at <strong>yourbusiness.com</strong>. The domain still belongs to you; we're just pointing its DNS at our hosting. The SSL certificate is active (you'll see a padlock in browsers), and Google has been told about your sitemap.</p>

      <h3>Pages we built</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Home</li>
        <li>About</li>
        <li>Services (and sub-pages for each major service)</li>
        <li>Service Area</li>
        <li>Contact (with a working Web3Forms form)</li>
        <li>Privacy Policy, Accessibility Statement, Terms of Use, Sitemap, and Style Guide; the operational pages that are always included</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What we handle going forward</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hosting.</strong> On a fast global CDN. Nothing for you to monitor.</li>
        <li><strong>SSL &amp; security.</strong> Renewed automatically. No vulnerable plugins because there are no plugins.</li>
        <li><strong>Uptime monitoring.</strong> We get notified if the site ever goes down. You don't need to watch it.</li>
        <li><strong>Content updates.</strong> Unlimited, included. Just email us what you want changed.</li>
        <li><strong>Emergency support.</strong> If something urgent breaks, we fix it. usually within an hour during business hours, same day on weekends.</li>
        <li><strong>Design refresh.</strong> Every two years we give the site a visual refresh to keep it current. No extra cost.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How to ask for changes</h3>
      <p>Email us at <strong>{{ site.email }}</strong>, call or text <strong>{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</strong>, or reply to any existing thread. Tell us what you want in plain language; you don't need to write it like a technical specification. A few examples:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>"Our new hours are 7am–6pm Monday through Saturday."</li>
        <li>"Add a new service page for gutter cleaning."</li>
        <li>"Please swap out the team photo on the About page."</li>
        <li>"We have a Grand Opening special; can we put a banner at the top for two weeks?"</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Usually we get it done the same business day. If it's bigger, we'll give you a timeline.</p>

      <h3>How to check your form submissions</h3>
      <p>Every message from your contact form comes straight to your business email. There's no dashboard to log into. If you want them routed somewhere different later, just say the word.</p>

      <h3>Your domain</h3>
      <p>You own it. If you've lost track of where you registered it, search your inbox for "domain renewal", that usually surfaces the registrar. If you're unsure, call us and we'll help you find it.</p>

      <h3>If you ever want to move on</h3>
      <p>We don't hold your domain or your content hostage. On the monthly plan we own the code, but your domain is yours, your content is yours, and we'll make a reasonable handover plan whenever you need one. No drama.</p>

      <h3>How to reach us (any hour)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <strong>{{ site.email }}</strong></li>
        <li>Phone/text: <strong>{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</strong></li>
        <li>Contact form on your own site (we get every message)</li>
      </ul>

      <footer style="margin-top:2.5rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted)">
        <p>That's the whole guide. Short on purpose; a website shouldn't need a manual. If anything ever isn't clear, we'd rather hear about it than have you figure it out alone.</p>
      </footer>

    </article>
